{"title":"chinese new year noodle therapy","link":"https://keningzhu.com/journal/chinese-new-years-noodle-therapy","date":1738904880000,"content":" \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2048\" height=\"2048\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/5e7ce8a0-75b7-4a1b-b47f-78ee2b75bff8/diaries-2.4.25.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n  <p>from my <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal\">weekly visual diaries</a></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n<hr />\n\n\n  <p>in the last years of moving around the world, I’ve grown a personal tradition of feeling extremely melancholy and sad on Chinese New Year’s, as if, in particular on that specific day, I feel the most amount of grief, and the wound of being a child of diaspora opens up like a cavern and swallows me whole. this year I realized — while making noodles — that I’m almost ready to confront this wound, and make some art about it. </p><p>btw, I highly recommend noodle therapy for all varieties of chinese-related homesickness. I followed a grandma’s recipe on the chinese app <a href=\"https://www.xiaohongshu.com/explore\" target=\"_blank\">RedNote</a>. </p><p>the last time I made noodles by hand was for my <a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal\" target=\"_blank\">30th birthday alone in santorini</a>, and while I enjoyed my meal very much, the noodles themselves were pretty bad. this time was much better.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=1000w\" width=\"3024\" height=\"4032\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/3ad20d32-fc1f-4c2d-a31b-d37a3d722b4c/IMG_3248.jpeg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong>on drawing process</strong></p><p>I drew this week’s diary mostly while laying horizontal on the couch and listening to an audiobook. I was pleasantly surprised by how relaxing and rejuvenated I felt afterwards. <br /><br />I’ve written previously about how drawing feels like finding my way in the dark. after I have a general sense of composition and shapes, I reach a place where it feels more or less “done” — as though the painting can finish itself, and just I doze off and let my hand do the work. <br /></p><p><strong>first sketch —</strong> </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                <img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=1000w\" width=\"2048\" height=\"2048\" srcset=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=100w 100w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=300w 300w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=500w 500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=750w 750w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=1000w 1000w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=1500w 1500w, https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/51e8148de4b01c1eb79c1977/82e64517-7a6d-4708-8c9a-2d55696b9100/diaries-2.4.25-1.jpg?format=2500w 2500w\" loading=\"lazy\" />\n\n            \n          \n        \n          \n        \n\n        \n      \n        </figure>\n      \n\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  <p><strong>week of january 27-31, 2025</strong></p><p><em>noodle therapy. every lunar new year’s spent in a foreign country, far away from family, friends and origins turns me into a black hole of familiar melancholy. this year - year 3 in istanbul - I made noodles by hand and felt 1000x better. K continues </em><a href=\"https://keningzhu.com/journal/leviathan-hydra-monster\" target=\"_blank\"><em>leviathan taming</em></a><em>.</em> </p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n    \n  \n    \n\n      \n\n      \n        <figure>\n          \n        \n        \n\n        \n          \n            \n          \n            \n                \n                \n                \n                \n                \n             